From ae708dc7c0ea9f8228c20cf8625e16469b6465df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ritesh Pandit <riteshp2001@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 10:51:37 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 134/140] fix(player): unify sheet spacing and preserve control
 placement

Shared player-sheet presentation
- Add reusable drag handles, title/section headers, and labeled tooltip
  actions with 48 dp targets. Keep title rows at a consistent minimum height.
- Use a common 640 dp maximum sheet width, bottom navigation insets, and
  bottom content spacing. Bound scrolling content below fixed headers while
  preserving swipe dismissal and reduced-motion behavior.
- Reuse the shared header, handle, and width in the native equalizer and
  audio-properties modals without changing their modal hosting.

Track selection and familiar tool placement
- Organize audio tracks, channel choices, and effects into clearer groups.
  Let channel choices wrap and use full-size switches for effects.
- Give track rows consistent gutters, minimum heights, semibold selection
  text, and room for metadata instead of bold italic labels.
- Preserve the previous action arrangement requested in review: equalizer
  and delay stay beside Add external audio; subtitle search, generation,
  styling, and delay tools stay beside Add external subtitles.
- Keep external subtitle translate/remove icons directly accessible instead
  of moving them into a menu. Retain the improved row and section spacing.
- Keep subtitle tools/progress/tracks in one scrolling list and bind the
  translation and live-caption bars to their corresponding progress values.
- Give online subtitle search a full-width input, a separate tool row, and
  season controls below the field. Scroll controls with results and reuse
  existing localized action labels.

Other player controls
- Align headings and spacing across visualizer, decoder, quality, chapters,
  bookmark editor, speed, aspect, audiobook, zoom, ambience, post-processing,
  scopes, and playlist sheets.
- Put chapter timestamps below names and correct current-chapter scrolling
  after moving its heading out of the list.
- Replace cramped speed-preset buttons with a stable icon slot, enlarge
  zoom controls, and remove scaled-down switches.
- Wrap aspect/post-processing choices, make scopes scroll, and remove the
  half-height caps from ambience and post-processing settings.
- Restore More's tools beside its title, with icon-only actions in portrait
  and labels in landscape, while keeping the improved section spacing.
- Expand portrait playlist space and use the shared list-mode width.
- Keep draggable panels at their previous 380 dp width cap. Retain safe-area
  padding, more portrait height, a larger drag target, bounded scrolling,
  and clamped horizontal positioning.

Drawer title and chapter availability
- Label the player control drawer Controls drawer using the existing string
  already translated in every supported locale.
- Always render configured BOOKMARKS_CHAPTERS and CURRENT_CHAPTER icons.
  When the combined chapter/bookmark list is empty, use the standard
  disabled tint and block both click and long-press actions instead of
  hiding the controls. Preserve populated-list behavior and the separate
  audio-player bookmark control.

Validation
- Focused editor diagnostics, source/resource/call-site inspection, and
  git diff --check passed; the static source graph was refreshed.
- No Android build, tests, formatter, emulator, or device UI checks were
  run under the standing static-only constraint. Compilation and device
  checks for orientation, IME, RTL/font scaling, TV focus, and gestures
  remain required. No generated schemas or changelog files were edited.
